enchilada: USB: the ECM data path survives a cable unplug/replug

After the cable was pulled while ue0 was in use and plugged into another port, the host
re-enumerated the phone, got NETWORK_CONNECTION and brought its link up, but the phone never
answered ARP until a reboot. Nothing ran on disconnect or bus reset except clearing the address:
ud.configured stayed true, so the new SET_CONFIGURATION(1) returned early from ud_configure()
(no Start New Configuration, no DEPCFG, bulk OUT not re-armed, data toggles not reset), and a
bulk IN frame queued for the old host that it never fetched left tx_busy set with no XferComplete
ever to come, so every later frame (ARP replies included) sat in or fell off the 32-entry TX ring.
Now a disconnect or USB reset event, and every SET_CONFIGURATION, does what Linux
dwc3_gadget_{disconnect,reset}_interrupt + f_ecm ecm_disable do: a forced END TRANSFER on each
data endpoint with a started transfer (resource index kept from START TRANSFER), the endpoints
taken out of DALEPENA, tx_busy cleared and the TX ring dropped, link down; a control transfer cut
off mid-way is ended and ep0 stalled and re-armed for SETUP (dwc3_ep0_reset_state). The new
SET_CONFIGURATION then configures and arms the endpoints from scratch and SET_INTERFACE alt 1 sends
NETWORK_CONNECTION and posts link up again. Completions arriving for bulk OUT while unconfigured
are not re-armed. The PHY, clocks and event buffer are left alone: the replug enumerated fine.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_usb.c
